  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Tekir</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An ancient settlement located at Tekir on the western tip of the modern Dat\u00e7a peninsula in Turkey (ancient Knidia), which extends from the southwest corner of Asia Minor. In the later fourth century BCE, it grew markedly, succeeding the site at Burgaz as the political center of the peninsula and attracting the name Cnidus to itself. It is often referred to as \"New Cnidus\" in recognition of this change.",
  "reprPoint": [
